From 59ce1307f6f69262eeb5bb174156428ce6611a4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hanoip <hanoip@localhost>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:04:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 165/194] net: qrtr: ns: wait for the HELLO before announcing
 servers

Since "net: qrtr: Send HELLO message on endpoint register" the core
sends our HELLO from a delayed work and rejects non-HELLO packets to the
node with -EAGAIN until it has gone out. When the remote says HELLO
first, announce_servers() hits that -EAGAIN, logs "failed to announce
new service" and stops; the name server no longer replies to HELLO, so
nothing announces the local servers again.

On Motorola hanoip (SM7150) the modem then never learns about rmtfs,
tqftpserv and pd-mapper, waits until its watchdog fires ("DOG detects
stalled initialization") and Wi-Fi never comes up: 3 of 6 boots.
Retry on -EAGAIN for up to a second instead.
---
 net/qrtr/ns.c | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/qrtr/ns.c b/net/qrtr/ns.c
index bcb090ee7..d4d77579c 100644
--- a/net/qrtr/ns.c
+++ b/net/qrtr/ns.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
  * Copyright (c) 2020, Linaro Ltd.
  */
 
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/qrtr.h>
 #include <linux/workqueue.h>
@@ -226,7 +227,21 @@ static int announce_servers(struct sockaddr_qrtr *sq)
 
 	/* Announce the list of servers registered in this node */
 	xa_for_each(&node->servers, index, srv) {
-		ret = service_announce_new(sq, srv);
+		int tries = 0;
+
+		/*
+		 * Our HELLO to a new node goes out from a delayed work in the
+		 * core; until then non-HELLO packets to it fail with -EAGAIN.
+		 * The remote can say HELLO first, so wait for ours instead of
+		 * dropping the announcements: nothing would retry them.
+		 */
+		do {
+			ret = service_announce_new(sq, srv);
+			if (ret != -EAGAIN)
+				break;
+			msleep(20);
+		} while (++tries < 50);
+
 		if (ret < 0) {
 			if (ret == -ENODEV)
 				continue;
